The Commit standing screen lists, scores and takes back session charges

tama standing gives each agent session a point for a commit in rustfmt's
form and takes one for a commit with a Rust file out of it, and below zero
every tool call of the session is refused; the app could not show any of it.
Policy, Commit standing lists every scored session, blocked ones first, with
its points and each charge's repository and files; Take back removes a
charge with the reason it was recorded in error; Score charges the commits
of a revision range made before they were scored. Each action runs tama
request standing/list, standing/score or standing/withdraw, the routes that
call the functions the CLI verbs call, and a refusal is shown in the
command's own words. The screen needs control access, as the Session screen
does. The README describes it.

Release and control identifiers are shown whole: the length they were cut
at was a number nobody declared, and a head cut at a guessed length can
name two identifiers.

The declared Swift format gate refuses the committed tree: thirteen sources
written before the gate checked them are out of swift-format's form. Their
committed versions are written in that form here, computed on the committed
tree exported into the build directory, so no session's uncommitted edit is
carried.

